{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1336160-which-renown-is-this","id":1336160,"title":"Which Renown is this?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-17T00:41:57-07:00","id":1336160,"title":"Which Renown is this?","content":"Not too much backstory here, but a situation I can't find a clear answer to. Running a mixed chronicle (that detail has only a little bearing on the situation) and the uratha was leading a charge. They had tracked down a vampire to his main haven (after finding a couple of decoys) and had him with his back to the wall. They fought past a group of armed guards and confronted the vamp by monitor since he'd hidden in his panic-room. With the gift of technology it was only going to be a moment before the hothead uratha was in and the hunt was over. However, the vampire revealed he'd anticipated this and had already sent a minion with an explosive to a crowded event where their informer was (they only knew of the evil this vamp was perpetrating due to another vamp). Faced with a choice and getting a bit of wise advice from his wolf-blooded companion, the uratha called off the hunt and raced to the event with just enough time to save dozens of innocents and their informant. When they returned to the hunt they discovered the vamp had used an escape vehicle and such to flee town. His minions don't know where since they were uninformed of his escape plan. So the vamp is in the wind now, and they have to start all over if they want to continue (though the things he was doing has been foiled here, at least).<br /> <br /> After the game the player approached me and asked if that decision was worth renown. I have to agree I feel like a tough decision and then personal sacrifice of letting prey go so he could go save dozens of people <i>should</i> be worth something. I'm just not sure which renown it is. At first glance I kind of thought Honor, but that seems more about fairness and equality, but it also seems to govern tough choices and sacrifice. Then I also though of Purity because of the Oath and respecting those beneath you (after all dozens of human innocents that need protecting certainly fit) but I wasn't sure if <i>rescuing</i> would be equivalent to <i>respecting?</i><br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm having a tough time of this so I though perhaps someone who knows werewolf a lot better would know what type of renown this would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T02:50:20-07:00","id":1336172,"title":"","content":"That sort of choice could easily be worth Cunning, Honor, or Wisdom, depending on the reasoning for the Uratha to abandon his prey in favor of dismantling the threat that the bomb represented because a bomb going off? Well, that's gonna bring a lot of heat to the area that would potentially threaten exposure for all supernaturals.<br /> <br /> And, the uratha shouldn't worry too much about the Vampire being in the wind. All he needs is the Impossible Spoor gift and I'm sure he'll pick up the trail again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T06:06:24-07:00","id":1336190,"title":"","content":"It's definitively not Purity, because he wasn't willing to sacrifice those people in order to finish the hunt.<br /> <br /> It's not Cunning or Wise, because the hunt could be already over and now he's given away any proposition at surprise, or even know the prey's whereabouts. What's more, you've shown that you can be manipulated in hostage situations. And was the hunt finished, the situation wouldn't repeat itself, like it very well could now.<br /> <br /> Neither it feels Glorious. This isn't something I would boast pridefully in a tribal gathering, for the reasons explained above.<br /> <br /> It feels more Honorable than anything assuming the informant was a packmate, or is about to be indicted into the hunt. Remember: Uratha feel no compunctions about killing on the hunt, be it directly, or indirectly. Their morality is blue and orange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:22:40-07:00","id":1336439,"title":"","content":"In essence, I would have simply contacted the relevant authorities to deal with the bomb and rid the world of another leech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T23:59:27-07:00","id":1336503,"title":"","content":"Yeah pointing out that the hunt could be over if he hadn't gone astray, definitely not Purity. That makes sense.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help and input, everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T07:41:34-07:00","id":1336552,"title":"","content":"I'd also say honor, if anything.<br /> <br /> But you could also argue against that, as in, the Uratha placed his own human moral code above his duty as an Uratha. Keep in mind renown is tied to an inhuman morality, it has nothing to do with the values renown embodies as seen from a human perspective but from a Forsaken/Uratha perspective.<br /> <br /> Edit: so I'd say it depends on the broader context of the hunt and why it was conducted. Was the Urathas main duty to hunt down the Vampire or was it to protect mortals from Vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","user":"nobby","date":". 09-18-2019, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T05:19:38-07:00","id":1336831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1336160-which-renown-is-this?p=1336552#post1336552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also say honor, if anything.<br /> <br /> But you could also argue against that, as in, the Uratha placed his own human moral code above his duty as an Uratha. Keep in mind renown is tied to an inhuman morality, it has nothing to do with the values renown embodies as seen from a human perspective but from a Forsaken/Uratha perspective.<br /> <br /> Edit: so I'd say it depends on the broader context of the hunt and why it was conducted. Was the Urathas main duty to hunt down the Vampire or was it to protect mortals from Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the caveat for it is if you do that to save a packmate. To do otherwise would be betrayal. If it was just a random human, even a contact, it doesn't even deserves that recognition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}